cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite ZMeta, cite the tagged release you relied on."
title: "ZMeta Specification and Reference Stack"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ZMeta contributors"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JTC-byte/zmeta-spec"
url: "https://github.com/JTC-byte/zmeta-spec"
version: "1.1.25"
date-released: "2026-08-13"
abstract: >-
  ZMeta is a free, open, transport-agnostic semantic standard for resilient
  ISR. It defines one event model, with governed validation, lineage, timing
  quality, confidence, profile projection, and policy adjudication, that
  heterogeneous sensors, analytics, gateways, and mission systems can share
  without changing what the data means. The repository has been publicly
  available since 2026-01-17 with dated, signed releases since 2026-01-18.
keywords:
  - ISR
  - interoperability
  - open specification
  - metadata
  - sensor fusion
